## Working as an agent

These hold whenever you work on your own, for example in a cloud session started from
an issue.

- **One issue, one branch, one PR.** Branch `<type>/<issue>-<slug>`, e.g.
  `feat/12-short-name`, cut from `dev`. Open the PR against `dev`; never merge it, and
  never push to `dev`, `staging` or `main` (they flow dev → staging → main, and
  promoting between them is the owner's). Always push with the branch named:
  `git push -u origin <your-branch>`. A bare `git push`, `git push origin` or
  `... HEAD` is denied, because it can't be told apart from a push to `dev`.
- **Stage is the handshake.** `Stage` is an org issue field. Find work with the
  GitHub MCP `list_issues` and
  `field_filters: [{field_name: "Stage", value: "Ready"}]`; GitHub search can't filter
  on it. An empty list means nothing is `Ready`. Set it with `issue_write` and
  `issue_fields: [{field_name: "Stage", field_option_name: "Working"}]`. Start only
  on `Ready`; set `Working` when you start. If you stop for any reason other than
  done, set `Asking` and say in a comment what the owner must do. When the PR is
  complete and green, set `In validation`. Never set `Ready`: that one is the
  owner's.
- **Never run the project's irreversible commands** (<database pushes, deploys,
  store submissions>). Write the change as a file and say in the PR that it needs
  applying. They are also denied in `.claude/settings.json`.
- **Recover before you stop.** When something fails, read the real error, try the
  alternatives (another tool, endpoint or source) and fix what's reversible. Set
  `Asking` only for what only the owner can do, and say what you tried, the
  alternative you prepared and your recommendation — never just "it doesn't work"
  ([agent-kit ADR 0010](https://github.com/ferrarolabs/agent-kit/blob/main/docs/decisions/0010-agents-recover-before-they-escalate.md)).
- **Plan on the issue, PR only when complete**
  ([agent-kit work flow](https://github.com/ferrarolabs/agent-kit/blob/main/docs/guides/work-flow.md),
  [agent-kit ADR 0023](https://github.com/ferrarolabs/agent-kit/blob/main/docs/decisions/0023-plan-on-the-issue-pr-only-when-complete.md)).
  Post the plan as a comment on the issue before any code, set `Asking` and stop.
  Resume when the owner sets `Ready` again, and do what their last comment says.
  Every change of plan is a new comment. Open the PR only when every "Done when" is
  met and you've used the result as a user would; no steps for the owner in it.
- **Product questions stop you: ask on the issue, not in a PR.** If the issue doesn't
  settle a product choice (scope, wording, who sees what), or only the owner can
  unblock it, don't guess: comment on the issue with the problem and the one thing
  the owner must do, set `Asking`, and stop. No partial PR.

## Definition of done

Who holds each line:

- Typecheck, lint, format, tests pass: `<the four commands joined with &&>` _(you,
  before saying done; CI on the PR)_
- New logic has a test where a test is meaningful _(you)_
- Decisions written down, contradicted docs updated in the same PR _(you write them;
  the owner checks in review)_
- <What only the owner can check: devices, real accounts, production> _(the owner —
  an agent session can't check these, so don't claim them; list in the PR what to
  try)_

## Recording decisions

Significant decisions → a new ADR in `docs/decisions/` (never edit an existing one;
supersede it). Everything smaller → a decision log. A decision that isn't written down is
lost by the next session.
